<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $47.7 mln May 19.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $47.7 mln May 19.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $47.7 million deficit on May 19 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 19</p>
<p>Exports: $306.2 million</p>
<p>Imports: $308.3 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $175.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $220.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $47.7 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.097 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.017 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.109 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.050 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.139 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
